WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.423 --> 00:00:01.510
(gunfire resounds)

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.640
- The world has been
watching both a geopolitical

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.410
and a humanitarian crisis
unfold between Israel

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.470
and the Palestinians in the
Gaza strip in recent days.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.840
Rockets from Gaza are striking in Israel,

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.300
and Israeli aircraft are pounding

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.650
a wide range of targets in Gaza.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.040
Civilians are dying,
and there's no clear way

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.670
to bring this dramatic escalation

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.634
of violence to a conclusion.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:24.510
(explosions resound)

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.550
In one sense, this
certainly is a new phase

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.910
in the decades-long conflict

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.040
between Israel and the Palestinians.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.620
But in other ways, this outbreak
is just more of the same

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.080
and a sign that the new
phase some had hoped for

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.800
in this long-running conflict
isn't at hand at all.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.720
First for starters, the outbreak shows

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.437
it isn't possible to simply
push the conflict between Israel

00:00:43.437 --> 00:00:45.840
and the Palestinians to the back burner

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.850
as the Trump administration tried.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.300
The Trump team thought Arab
states had grown so tired

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.800
of the Palestinian question

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.180
that they would merely
sidestep Palestinian demands

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.280
for their own state and return of lands

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.630
under Israeli control
and concentrate instead

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:02.300
on making peace with Israel
and confronting Iran.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.140
- When you came into office,
Iran was on the march.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.723
Because of your leadership,
Iran is now on the run.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.480
- And that worked to
some extent as Bahrain,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.920
the United Arab Emirates,
Morocco, and Sudan

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.330
all established formal ties with Israel.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.070
The hope was that the Palestinian issue

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.040
would just fade in importance
as the Sunni Arab states

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.850
focused instead on confronting Iran.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.380
But as the new violence illustrates

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.750
and as diplomats have
learned over the decades,

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.350
the Palestinian question has a way

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.580
of rearing its head over and over again

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.660
often when you least expect.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.780
Second, this crisis shows
that it won't be as easy

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.130
to push Israeli Prime
Minister Benjamin Netanyahu

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:42.890
out of power as his critics
at home and abroad had hoped.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:45.300
After Israel's fourth election
in two years recently,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.360
Mr. Netanyahu had been unable
to form a new government

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.170
and his main opponent had
been given the chance,

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:54.230
but the current crisis is
pushing domestic politics aside

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:57.210
in Israel, and likely will
prompt some Israelis to rally

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.000
around their prime minister
in a time of duress.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.390
That might actually extend

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:04.290
Mr. Netanyahu's long streak in power.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.740
And finally, this crisis shows

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.410
that it isn't really
possible, at least not yet,

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.450
to detach Iran from the
broader Palestinian problem.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.930
The extremist group Hamas
is firing the rockets

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.040
that are landing on Israel,

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.240
and Iran is the main
international supporter of Hamas.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.700
And it was Iranian know-how
that largely helped

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.560
Hamas figure out how to produce on its own

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.630
the rockets it is now firing.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.030
So the current crisis is showing

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.010
that the continued
importance of the alliance

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.730
between Iran and Hamas
is as strong as ever.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:35.120
And indeed, this could end
up deepening that alliance.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.920
In sum, while the crisis is
a dramatic new escalation

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.210
in tensions between Israel
and the Palestinians,

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.990
it also is in many ways
showing the old dynamics

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:46.673
are still in place and maybe
even growing more entrenched.

00:02:47.582 --> 00:02:51.082
(soft instrumental music)

